  "holistic_F_N": -1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires reporting all thermal incidents within 24 hours and customer notice within 72 hours. S2 sets a 55 °C test with a 5% failure limit and per-model results to customers, but exceeding the limit triggers corrective action and possible sales restriction rather than an automatic sales stop. S3 mandates new-unit shut-off within 12 months and retrofits within 6 years with a feasibility escape. S4 requires built-in fire suppression within 36 months. S5 sets an 8 per 100,000 recall trigger but lets the regulator choose corrective action instead of recall, with prompt customer notices."
